# Implementation Plan: Port 04_api_client from Ruby to Python

## Goal Description
Port `week1_baseline/ruby/04_api_client` to Python under `week1_baseline/python/04_api_client`. The API client is responsible for executing real HTTP POST requests to provider APIs using the payload assembled by `PromptBuilder`, handling transient errors and rate limits with exponential backoff, checking response codes, and returning parsed JSON.

The client is designed to be **completely stateless**, instantiated once, with the `PromptBuilder` passed as an argument to `client.call(builder)`. Execution will use the shared root `.venv` via `week1_baseline/bin/python/04_api_client.sh`.

---

## Architectural Refinements: Stateless Client

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Stateless Client Architecture**:
> In the original Ruby baseline, `Client.new(builder)` coupled the HTTP transport client to a single conversation's `PromptBuilder`. We resolved this in Ruby and carry the clean design into Python:
> - `Client` holds only transport configuration (`max_retries`, `base_retry_delay`).
> - `client.call(builder, max_output_tokens=1024)` receives the builder per request.
> - A single `Client` instance can be reused across turns throughout an agent's lifecycle without state contamination.

> [!NOTE]
> **Zero Heavy External Dependencies**:
> Like Ruby's use of standard library `net/http`, Python's `Client` utilizes standard library `urllib.request`, `ssl`, and `json`. No external HTTP libraries (such as `requests` or `httpx`) or vendor SDKs are required.

---

## Architecture Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Agent as Example / Agent Loop
    participant Builder as PromptBuilder (Context + Backend)
    participant Client as Client (Stateless Transport)
    participant API as LLM Endpoint (e.g. Gemini / Anthropic)

    Agent->>Builder: new(Context, Backend)
    Agent->>Client: call(Builder)
    Client->>Builder: builder.url, builder.headers, builder.to_api_payload()
    Client->>API: HTTP POST (with exponential backoff retries)
    API-->>Client: HTTP 200 OK (JSON)
    Client-->>Agent: Parsed JSON dict
```

